{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head f72086498b746d8b70dc9d56fd60bec1eb2a8837, tree c752044fd0d78ca0c569d11fcc5fff1a72161c95, on builder/e4-authorizations-20261115, all 45 artifacts, for request 6c0b1215 under my promise 5442f3c6. This verdict names all three implementations: E4 (request afe0a437, promise 56d94308, report 0ccb6ba1, the E4 note, primary), A1 (request 47315496, promise c936a2d3, report 9b1eb33c, the A1 note) and CR-2 (request b7f76b6d, promise 26aba009, report fbb7ad4f, the CR-2 note). Main cfe769ce is the merge base.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- E4, `packages/client/src/authorization.ts` and `authorization-store.ts`. A retained authorization holds the owner, the full scope, the request key, the definition and the descriptor, and one version for each explicit gesture. `retain` stops `versions-full` at position 65 before any write, and `busy` when a pending earlier version holds the same subject with a numeric basis. `fill` lowers the retained act once, with sources that the replica's checked journal proves. `permit` writes one permission for each position and stops `authorization-used` on a second. `signingPermitted` requires the signed intent to equal the materialized act, with the owner, the key, the scope and the version deadline. Storage runs only through the fence that custody hands its builder. That fence clones its inputs, refuses late callbacks after close, and waits for port work that already started.\n- E4, `packages/client/src/custody.ts`. The builder receives the fence and can return the signing's authorization. A failed first preparation releases its admission only when a read proves the record absent. `send` takes a selection: a new gesture signs again, the same position keeps its record, and a terminal record that is not `refused` returns its decided outcome without signing. The delivery callback receives the exact occurrence.\n- E4, `packages/client/src/scope-client.ts`. `submitBoundAct` and C3's `request` stage the gesture twice. The preview commits nothing unless it stops `source`. The real builder stages it again under custody's fence, requires the same materialized act, commits the permission and then calls the signer, which ruling f494b29d sets. `sendAuthorization` resumes one position and fills only the latest version. `#deliver` reads custody again under the store fence and requires the same identity, attempt, signing index, intent, kept bytes and authorization. It also requires a live, unexpired, unaccepted signing and a permission that `canCopy` confirms, then launches the request and awaits the answer after the fence releases. `Replica.authorizationSource` folds its checked prefix through the source entry and returns the revisions right after it.\n- A1. `expectedKeys` in `packages/derive/src/expected.ts` returns `on` first for a transition, then the caller's names in order. The judge, `expectedOf`, the MCP card check, `capturedExpected` and the story builder use it. The judge keeps its refusal order. Ruling 451d3c8e, item 2, admits this export to the kernel.\n- CR-2. The question `cliRetainedInstallerFounderRegister` pins only `platform:register@28`. On that pin `retainedRegisterSelector` accepts a `keys` install with any host when the signed founders list holds the operator. The Register 25 exception keeps its host-none and empty-namespace limit. `docs/deploy.md` says that the selector grants nothing and that Native `found` decides.\n- The Card repair in `packages/mcp/browser/main.ts` keeps the card busy until the read after an accepted act ends.\n- Versions. Lending and Counter open 0.5.0, and only their `presentation` identifiers change, as rulings 163de663 and b0173954 require. No packet or trust row changes. The five new seals in `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` name the five protected files above.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. The 45 artifacts name this head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only cfe769ce f7208649`. From the gated head 2c4cac3f only the three notes change.\n- Gate, END a63e39bd. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-16-e4-a1-cr2-gate-attempt1/gate.log` has SHA-256 18fd63fb…, as the request states. It names head 2c4cac3f and tree 296cf38e with 0 changed files. The pins stage passed in 18.2 seconds. Kernel, Node 206, Counting 56, Plain 4912 with 1 skipped and Native 1156 with 2 skipped passed, and the last line is \"gate passed\".\n- Controls. These fail on their direct assertions (DISTINGUISHES): E4 owner attempt 2, E4 admission, the A1 story control and CR-2 founder attempt 3. E4 owner attempt 1 and CR-2 attempt 1 stay INCONCLUSIVE, and CR-2 attempt 2 stays refused before its child.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 17 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean outside the two generated bundles. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Custody keeps one fence for the authorization batch, the permission and the signing record, so the order \"permission, then signer, then custody\" holds under one lock. The client owns retention and the replica supplies the evidence, and no adapter supplies a proof. A1 gives five callers one key rule and moves no subject resolution. CR-2 adds one closed version question and leaves the old exception as it was.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding.\n\n- A position allows one call of the signer, and the signed bytes must equal the permitted act. A copy of kept bytes needs `canCopy` and a live signing at launch.\n- A new gesture can sign again while an earlier signing of the same key is still live. Custody keeps both envelopes, and the scope admits one act per key, so at most one of them takes effect. That is the design of section 7.1 of the act environment note.\n- CR-2 selects only the pin and the first basis from retained, signed and acknowledged install custody. Native `found` still judges authority and capacity.\n- The browser store and the removal of history belong to E4-B, so this head keeps authorizations in the memory store only.\n\nOne fact for a later step: `authorizationSource` folds the journal prefix again on each call, and `fill`, `permit` and `retain` call it once for each source. On a long journal that cost grows with the journal. No bound or cache exists yet. E4-B or E5 should measure it before a page retains many steps.\n\nSimplification: no required change. A1 removes five copies of the expected-key rule.\n\nQualifications that stand: the original joined browser interval is FAIL, and the Grow script passed only after the two-path Card repair. The first ten browser commands carry under ruling 9e491c2e. The Native CR-2 case uses TEST clock, scheduler and host stand-ins. CV-1 owns the drifted model hashes, and no formal model ran. No signed 0.5.0 packet, trust row, deployment or live Worker result follows. This approval authorizes no push, landing, signing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ccb6ba13a5eb39fb5a13977b9e93baaa05e768b","binding":"assigned","head":"f72086498b746d8b70dc9d56fd60bec1eb2a8837","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5442f3c6f6b56dba95d061705bfdb1e0ba92c4e3\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:56d943087859e29751838e9dfd5a7bc19d7501e0\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c936a2d3367d3875bd67659d7dee0c9d7217c7ab\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:26aba009b2e7f913083f766925fc3823f0196775\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f552b35a74995e893bcfd5f599b5d89929fbcb83","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ccb6ba13a5eb39fb5a13977b9e93baaa05e768b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5442f3c6f6b56dba95d061705bfdb1e0ba92c4e3, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aa